WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.707 --> 00:00:06.469
The internet has changed the way we live.

00:00:07.811 --> 00:00:09.392
It has changed the way we work,

00:00:09.873 --> 00:00:10.653
the way we shop,

00:00:11.194 --> 00:00:12.695
and even the way we date.

00:00:13.496 --> 00:00:16.317
It has also changed the way we kill.

00:00:17.919 --> 00:00:26.166
I'm Donald McIntyre and I'm on a quest to explore the dark side of our online world where one click can lead to murder.

00:00:27.703 --> 00:00:31.366
The internet and social media has been a godsend to online predators.

00:00:31.546 --> 00:00:31.786
Why?

00:00:31.826 --> 00:00:33.527
Because of the speed in which they can,

00:00:33.747 --> 00:00:33.967
one,

00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:35.348
create fake profiles,

00:00:35.408 --> 00:00:35.810
but two,

00:00:35.909 --> 00:00:36.769
access victims.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.634
I'll be investigating some of the most disturbing crimes in recent history,

00:00:42.153 --> 00:00:45.316
where the internet and social media have been used to trick,

00:00:45.656 --> 00:00:47.857
torture and kill innocent victims,

00:00:48.177 --> 00:00:51.640
lured into a virtual world where nothing is as it seems.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.944
Clearly she did not realise the person she was talking to online was...

00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:57.243
the man who was going to kill her.

00:00:58.545 --> 00:01:00.164
In this programme,

00:01:00.265 --> 00:01:06.807
15-year-old schoolboy Safian Belamawadin was stabbed to death by a vicious mob in the middle of the London rush hour.

00:01:07.906 --> 00:01:15.128
It was a crime that shocked the nation and led to the largest murder prosecution in the history of the Metropolitan Police.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.810
The night before Safian's stabbing,

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.691
his teenage killers were communicating feverishly online.

00:01:22.251 --> 00:01:23.932
Did these social media messages...

00:01:24.291 --> 00:01:28.879
wind the youngsters up into a frenzy where they felt compelled to commit murder.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.651
Tensions and fights between rival schools are nothing new,

00:02:10.032 --> 00:02:11.774
and most are over pretty quickly.

00:02:12.153 --> 00:02:14.395
They certainly rarely end up in murder.

00:02:14.757 --> 00:02:18.039
But in the case of London schoolboys Sufian Belamouadn,

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.881
that's exactly what happened.

00:02:24.024 --> 00:02:24.884
March 25th,

00:02:24.965 --> 00:02:27.966
2010 at Victoria train station,

00:02:28.387 --> 00:02:33.030
15 year old Sofian was killed by a gang of knife wielding teenagers.

00:02:34.591 --> 00:02:36.872
As crowds of horrified commuters looked on,

00:02:37.293 --> 00:02:38.913
this conscientious young schoolboy

00:02:38.953 --> 00:02:44.714
boy found himself on the front line of a pitched battle between pupils from rival schools.

00:02:47.315 --> 00:02:49.756
Unarmed and alone against the baying mob,

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:55.697
he was stabbed and kicked to death in a ferocious attack that lasted just a matter of seconds.

00:03:07.111 --> 00:03:13.937
How did a petty school rivalry turn into a bloodbath in this space of just 24 hours?

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:22.903
I'm on my way to West London where Sofian and his family lived and where Sofian went to school.

00:03:23.364 --> 00:03:31.591
I want to investigate the role social media played in his murder and how he got caught up in the violence that was to cost him his life.

00:03:37.836 --> 00:03:40.159
Safian Belmawadden grew up in Acton,

00:03:40.539 --> 00:03:41.221
West London.

00:03:44.025 --> 00:03:45.045
One of four siblings,

00:03:45.247 --> 00:03:46.968
he had a brother and two sisters.

00:03:48.471 --> 00:03:52.897
Safian's mother was the daughter of Moroccan immigrants who arrived in Britain in the

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:54.019
1970s.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.808
He came from a very loving family.

00:03:57.429 --> 00:03:58.909
He observed Ramadan.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.249
He was quite a devout Muslim.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:01.910
And to all intents and purposes,

00:04:01.911 --> 00:04:05.371
he looked like a young boy who was going to go off and have a successful,

00:04:05.731 --> 00:04:06.831
happy life.

00:04:08.872 --> 00:04:10.733
Sufian was a lively boy.

00:04:11.733 --> 00:04:12.973
He was always smiling,

00:04:13.612 --> 00:04:14.133
always happy.

00:04:15.194 --> 00:04:16.293
He was a family person.

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.235
It was all happy memories,

00:04:18.735 --> 00:04:19.495
never bad memories.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:19.855
Obviously,

00:04:19.855 --> 00:04:20.875
we had our ups and downs.

00:04:20.876 --> 00:04:21.975
We are brothers and sisters.

00:04:23.072 --> 00:04:25.033
But we used to go bike riding,

00:04:25.813 --> 00:04:28.875
he used to play football with me when we were younger outside the house.

00:04:30.237 --> 00:04:30.918
I was like,

00:04:30.997 --> 00:04:31.658
I'm really...

00:04:31.758 --> 00:04:32.058
Literally,

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:32.718
I'm really him.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.581
So every time I walk out,

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:37.742
I get told that

00:04:38.243 --> 00:04:39.103
I look like him.

00:04:39.664 --> 00:04:40.384
Even at dinner,

00:04:41.145 --> 00:04:42.806
I get told that I move like him.

00:04:43.967 --> 00:04:46.409
So he's forever going to be a part of me,

00:04:46.789 --> 00:04:48.091
no matter how old I get.

00:04:53.939 --> 00:04:55.425
Sofyan went to this school,

00:04:55.706 --> 00:04:58.896
which is then called the Henry Compton School for Boys.

00:04:58.896 --> 00:04:59.980
The teacher said he was in...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.980
...industrious and smart.

00:05:02.021 --> 00:05:05.045
He was considered polite and popular among his peers.

00:05:05.045 --> 00:05:06.766
And he was also a talented sportsman.

00:05:07.065 --> 00:05:09.649
He played centre half in his local football team.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.351
His father was convinced that had he lived,

00:05:13.471 --> 00:05:15.613
Sothian would have gone on and played for England.

00:05:15.634 --> 00:05:17.115
He certainly wanted to play for England.

00:05:18.196 --> 00:05:21.119
And Chelsea and a number of clubs were interested in him.

00:05:24.819 --> 00:05:29.923
How did things go so wrong for this teenager with such a promising life ahead of him?

00:05:30.702 --> 00:05:34.425
What exactly were the events that led to Sofian's tragic death?

00:05:44.536 --> 00:05:51.285
For several months there had been an ongoing feud between Safian's Henry Compton friends and students from another school,

00:05:51.646 --> 00:05:52.846
St Charles College,

00:05:53.168 --> 00:05:54.930
following a fight at a party.

00:06:10.487 --> 00:06:12.790
Things came to a head on March 24th,

00:06:13.189 --> 00:06:17.673
when pupils from both schools clashed again outside a McDonald's restaurant.

00:06:21.415 --> 00:06:25.057
I think some chips have been thrown and things have obviously clearly...

00:06:25.697 --> 00:06:27.899
escalated into a bit of a fight.

00:06:28.878 --> 00:06:32.420
A friend of Sofian's threw a punch at one of the rival gang.

00:06:32.421 --> 00:06:32.500
Once.

00:06:32.502 --> 00:06:32.620
Oh

00:06:35.581 --> 00:06:37.141
And for the St Charles kids,

00:06:37.462 --> 00:06:40.163
this loss of face was too much to bear.

00:06:40.743 --> 00:06:40.863
The

00:06:41.303 --> 00:06:50.687
St Charles school gang decided that they were going to mount a major assault the following day to put their rivals out of the picture once and for all.

00:06:58.182 --> 00:06:59.663
As soon as the fight was over,

00:07:00.043 --> 00:07:04.487
messages started to fly back and forth over Facebook and Blackberry Messenger.

00:07:05.187 --> 00:07:08.930
Well back in the day the Blackberry was the phone of choice for businessmen,

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.492
criminals and indeed teenagers.

00:07:11.793 --> 00:07:12.954
It was easy to use.

00:07:13.214 --> 00:07:16.917
the messages were highly encrypted and very difficult to intercept.

00:07:17.358 --> 00:07:22.902
The kids from St Charles used the BlackBerry Messenger to set up a closed group so they can chat amongst themselves.

00:07:23.203 --> 00:07:25.304
When the news came through of the attack on McDonald's,

00:07:25.585 --> 00:07:28.607
they used this app to orchestrate their revenge.

00:07:29.627 --> 00:07:32.050
We need to understand that at that time period,

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.971
the Blackberry was very much an image for the gangster,

00:07:35.972 --> 00:07:37.413
an image for the street person,

00:07:37.592 --> 00:07:40.194
an image for the urban collective,

00:07:40.754 --> 00:07:43.356
an image for the one that's looking for the surrogate family.

00:07:43.637 --> 00:07:43.837
Why?

00:07:43.897 --> 00:07:44.497
Because it means...

00:07:44.558 --> 00:07:59.858
that he or she can set up a group chat that his friends may not need to be involved in it and it's a way of continuing to promote that negative lifestyle or that negative behavior without another group knowing who you're talking about

00:08:03.211 --> 00:08:08.013
Bad blood already existed between the pupils from Soffian School and those from St.

00:08:08.072 --> 00:08:08.533
Charles,

00:08:08.874 --> 00:08:11.675
following a bust-up at a party some months earlier.

00:08:12.134 --> 00:08:20.016
And the scuffle outside McDonald's in Victoria was simply the latest incident in a simmering feud between the teenagers from both schools.

00:08:20.417 --> 00:08:22.978
And while that incident may have seemed trivial,

00:08:23.257 --> 00:08:27.778
it was to prove to be the key trigger for the tragic events that followed.

00:08:30.783 --> 00:08:31.043
On the

00:08:31.624 --> 00:08:33.447
25th of March 2010,

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:34.848
London schoolboy

00:08:35.208 --> 00:08:40.855
Safian Belamawadden was murdered in broad daylight in a fight between two rival schools.

00:08:42.197 --> 00:08:51.986
I'm on a journey to find out how a minor scuffle between these two groups of teenagers could have escalated into a murderous rampage in just 24 hours.

00:08:56.343 --> 00:08:57.125
The day before,

00:08:57.325 --> 00:09:02.967
a fight had broken out between Sofyan's friends from the Henry Compton School and pupils from St.

00:09:03.028 --> 00:09:05.049
Charles Arrival Schools.

00:09:08.871 --> 00:09:11.193
News of the fight spread like wildfire.

00:09:11.273 --> 00:09:13.114
on social media as the St.

00:09:13.154 --> 00:09:16.435
Charles pupils took to Facebook and Blackberry Messenger.

00:09:17.295 --> 00:09:18.996
They were desperate for retribution,

00:09:19.356 --> 00:09:24.017
and it wasn't long before they were discussing when and where they would exact their revenge.

00:09:24.617 --> 00:09:26.498
The students suggested using Nanks,

00:09:26.998 --> 00:09:28.379
slang for knives.

00:09:29.908 --> 00:09:35.580
This language is all too common among teenagers who find themselves involved in gang activity.

00:09:36.682 --> 00:09:37.143
But the St.

00:09:37.182 --> 00:09:40.509
Charles students weren't your average thugs or gangsters.

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:57.274
I've been able to find the police notes on the case compiled after the killers were caught and they revealed something really interesting.

00:09:57.755 --> 00:09:57.896
Now,

00:09:58.235 --> 00:09:59.920
most offenders go through various...

00:10:00.059 --> 00:10:03.880
stages of criminality and the police call this the forensic escalator.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:10.782
Typically an offender might start with petty crime before graduating in stages to more serious offences.

00:10:12.722 --> 00:10:20.283
But in this case most of the young teenagers prosecuted in relation to Sofian's murder had no criminal record whatsoever.

00:10:20.884 --> 00:10:27.225
What was surprising was that the majority of those taking part in the attack were actually well brought up.

00:10:27.706 --> 00:10:30.408
...industrious pupils interested in learning...

00:10:30.528 --> 00:10:33.513
...interested in getting qualifications from decent backgrounds.

00:10:34.774 --> 00:10:37.157
These were the children who were going to make it.

00:10:37.277 --> 00:10:38.719
They were going to go to university.

00:10:38.818 --> 00:10:41.542
They were making the effort to get to school on time...

00:10:41.842 --> 00:10:43.825
...to take two buses across London,

00:10:44.185 --> 00:10:45.407
there and back each day.

00:10:46.956 --> 00:10:50.857
But even for teenagers as studious and well-behaved as those from St.

00:10:50.898 --> 00:10:51.377
Charles,

00:10:51.717 --> 00:10:53.658
the allure of the gangster lifestyle,

00:10:53.938 --> 00:10:56.799
glamorized online and in modern youth culture,

00:10:57.019 --> 00:10:58.841
can still be extremely strong.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.981
The profiles that you see on some of these people's,

00:11:02.261 --> 00:11:02.501
you know,

00:11:03.202 --> 00:11:04.082
Facebook accounts,

00:11:04.423 --> 00:11:06.403
it's all about the gangster image.

00:11:07.223 --> 00:11:07.745
To them,

00:11:09.164 --> 00:11:10.846
this lifestyle seems fun.

00:11:12.567 --> 00:11:15.827
And to many of these kids who were doing well at school...

00:11:16.416 --> 00:11:17.737
And a lot of people are always saying,

00:11:17.877 --> 00:11:19.057
but they were doing well at school.

00:11:19.098 --> 00:11:19.999
This is not about that.

00:11:20.059 --> 00:11:21.158
This is about fitting in.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:22.700
To young people,

00:11:23.021 --> 00:11:27.244
fitting in often means being part of something bigger than their ordinary,

00:11:27.464 --> 00:11:28.543
everyday lives.

00:11:29.325 --> 00:11:32.127
The fight with the Henry Compton kids gave the St.

00:11:32.167 --> 00:11:34.268
Charles gang something to focus on,

00:11:34.629 --> 00:11:38.912
a flashpoint that would rapidly cause the situation to boil over.

00:11:39.652 --> 00:11:42.214
These kids may not have woke up one morning and said,

00:11:42.215 --> 00:11:42.454
you know,

00:11:42.554 --> 00:11:43.335
I'm going to murder.

00:11:43.774 --> 00:11:44.975
But what happens is...

00:11:45.316 --> 00:11:47.576
is when people are hyping a situation up,

00:11:47.836 --> 00:11:50.317
you're no longer thinking whether the person's going to be killed or not.

00:11:50.557 --> 00:11:51.258
You're just thinking,

00:11:51.358 --> 00:11:52.577
I have to be a part of that.

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:05.861
I've been reading up on the events leading up to Zofian's murder when he was set upon by an angry mob of teenagers.

00:12:07.741 --> 00:12:08.762
But who were they?

00:12:09.682 --> 00:12:14.663
And what made them go from zero to ten on the forensic escalator so quickly?

00:12:16.608 --> 00:12:18.990
These kids got involved because they were inflamed,

00:12:19.009 --> 00:12:19.711
they were hyped,

00:12:19.811 --> 00:12:20.531
they were gassed.

00:12:20.551 --> 00:12:22.233
These are the words these young people use.

00:12:22.513 --> 00:12:23.994
And they were whipped up into a frenzy.

00:12:24.014 --> 00:12:25.035
It's quite straightforward.

00:12:25.355 --> 00:12:29.599
And it's not hard to do that when you've got a social media platform that is out there free.

00:12:32.461 --> 00:12:34.483
Social media is a very strange animal.

00:12:35.263 --> 00:12:39.927
We know that individuals on social media say things,

00:12:40.206 --> 00:12:40.927
do things,

00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:44.730
support things that they wouldn't dream of doing in the real world.

00:12:46.243 --> 00:12:48.404
We know many cases where individuals,

00:12:48.484 --> 00:12:49.304
quite rational,

00:12:49.404 --> 00:12:49.684
sane,

00:12:49.745 --> 00:12:50.925
likeable individuals,

00:12:51.346 --> 00:12:56.227
do very silly or strange or outrageous things online and then regret it afterwards.

00:12:57.107 --> 00:13:11.313
I think we can clearly see that social media and text messaging worked like a magnifier to increase the significance and the importance of what would have been otherwise written off as a spat,

00:13:11.553 --> 00:13:11.953
as a blip.

00:13:11.973 --> 00:13:12.493
Bloody knows.

00:13:13.314 --> 00:13:18.037
And something calamitous had to happen as a result of all of that activity.

00:13:18.598 --> 00:13:22.821
Without social media and without the key players involved,

00:13:23.041 --> 00:13:26.303
they wouldn't have got whipped up into this fury that happened.

00:13:27.003 --> 00:13:31.307
We have the leaders who are talking about being tooled up,

00:13:31.647 --> 00:13:32.687
what they're going to do tomorrow,

00:13:33.008 --> 00:13:34.128
somebody's going to die.

00:13:34.649 --> 00:13:35.489
And without that,

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.531
it wouldn't have had the same momentum.

00:13:40.596 --> 00:13:42.157
As night fell on March

00:13:42.837 --> 00:13:47.221
24th, the BlackBerry and Facebook messages continued to fly back and forth.

00:13:48.361 --> 00:13:49.283
Throughout that evening,

00:13:49.383 --> 00:13:50.104
dozens of St.

00:13:50.144 --> 00:13:50.524
Charles'

00:13:50.583 --> 00:14:00.432
students were communicating on social media and their tone became increasingly fevered as they discussed their desperate need to exact some kind of revenge.

00:14:00.831 --> 00:14:03.754
The chief among those voices was Samson Odigbune,

00:14:04.095 --> 00:14:04.215
who,

00:14:04.274 --> 00:14:05.796
unlike most of his fellow students,

00:14:06.076 --> 00:14:07.538
actually was known to the police.

00:14:07.918 --> 00:14:08.639
At that stage,

00:14:08.658 --> 00:14:10.000
she was currently on bail.

00:14:10.279 --> 00:14:12.760
for the brandishing of a samurai sword on a bus.

00:14:14.861 --> 00:14:17.363
Odegbune was a criminal in the making.

00:14:17.763 --> 00:14:19.844
Even at the age of

00:14:20.524 --> 00:14:27.267
17, he had previous convictions and was on a spiral that was going to take him up to being a serious criminal.

00:14:28.267 --> 00:14:29.707
Another key agitator was

00:14:30.128 --> 00:14:31.408
18-year-old Victoria

00:14:31.908 --> 00:14:32.528
Osoteku.

00:14:33.789 --> 00:14:38.451
Victoria Osoteku was one of the most troubling figures in the whole case.

00:14:38.491 --> 00:14:39.251
She was clearly...

00:14:39.771 --> 00:14:44.453
A key figure in the whole plan to have this pitched battle.

00:14:44.733 --> 00:14:46.214
And though she didn't have a criminal record,

00:14:46.254 --> 00:14:48.114
she'd clearly come from quite a troubled background.

00:14:48.514 --> 00:14:51.396
She'd been taken in and out of care at an early age.

00:14:51.696 --> 00:14:53.516
She'd had very little contact with her mother,

00:14:53.697 --> 00:14:54.737
who'd been a drug addict.

00:14:56.117 --> 00:14:58.038
Yet when she arrived at school,

00:14:58.698 --> 00:14:59.159
she was...

00:15:00.019 --> 00:15:00.620
A good pupil.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:01.541
She was interested.

00:15:01.581 --> 00:15:02.780
She was engaged.

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.361
She was doing A-levels,

00:15:04.802 --> 00:15:06.423
but she was also a bully.

00:15:08.504 --> 00:15:13.125
Osoteku adopted a social media alter ego with the name of Missy Mafia,

00:15:13.525 --> 00:15:16.187
in which she portrayed herself as a young gangster.

00:15:16.907 --> 00:15:20.149
People who'd been in her classes would back that up.

00:15:20.249 --> 00:15:23.070
They said that she did have a reputation for being a bit of a bully,

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:27.412
and she clearly enjoyed exerting a control and influence over others.

00:15:31.032 --> 00:15:32.493
Following the fight between the St.

00:15:32.533 --> 00:15:36.014
Charles gang and the Henry Compton kids outside McDonald's,

00:15:36.494 --> 00:15:42.396
Osoteku spent the night feverishly chatting with her friends on Facebook and BlackBerry Messenger.

00:15:43.436 --> 00:15:48.437
Her messages became increasingly strident as she demanded swift and brutal revenge.

00:15:49.157 --> 00:15:51.817
She urged her schoolmates to come to school the next day,

00:15:52.418 --> 00:15:53.018
tooled up.

00:15:53.739 --> 00:15:55.419
Osoteku was busy on

00:15:55.879 --> 00:15:58.540
Facebook and Twitter and texting.

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:03.944
urging people on to take this matter up to a serious level.

00:16:04.225 --> 00:16:07.067
It wasn't good enough that there was going to be just a set two.

00:16:08.028 --> 00:16:10.389
This had to be a serious level of violence.

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.051
So she was saying to them,

00:16:12.652 --> 00:16:13.773
must bring weapons.

00:16:16.035 --> 00:16:20.579
Some of the St Charles pupils were also in touch with students from Soffian School.

00:16:21.219 --> 00:16:23.521
Threats and counter-threats were made.

00:16:24.122 --> 00:16:26.564
And by the time everyone went to bed that night...

00:16:26.803 --> 00:16:30.426
plans for the next day's violence were well advanced.

00:16:41.096 --> 00:16:43.298
I found out that most of the St Charles'

00:16:43.397 --> 00:16:46.360
pupils were regarded as a credit to their school.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:50.844
Many had achieved high grades and were expected to go on to great things.

00:16:51.184 --> 00:16:54.587
But why did so many of these bright young students...

00:16:54.888 --> 00:16:59.051
worked themselves up into such a frantic feeding frenzy on social media.

00:17:00.091 --> 00:17:08.376
I've come to meet criminologist Dr Elizabeth Yardley and psychologist Mike Berry to find out why events escalated so quickly.

00:17:09.158 --> 00:17:10.439
When you get on the internet,

00:17:10.778 --> 00:17:12.339
you lose a lot of control.

00:17:12.579 --> 00:17:12.720
Now,

00:17:13.079 --> 00:17:15.382
I write a message that's lacking control.

00:17:15.701 --> 00:17:16.383
You receive it,

00:17:16.384 --> 00:17:17.383
you pass it on to other people.

00:17:17.683 --> 00:17:19.684
The control element just goes.

00:17:19.985 --> 00:17:20.925
You become disinhibited.

00:17:21.145 --> 00:17:24.107
It's like being drunk without having to take the alcohol.

00:17:24.768 --> 00:17:25.249
In essence,

00:17:25.308 --> 00:17:27.110
it doesn't feel quite real.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.230
You're more disinhibited,

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:30.653
you say things you otherwise wouldn't say face to face,

00:17:30.913 --> 00:17:32.535
but it doesn't seem to have the same impact.

00:17:32.934 --> 00:17:33.095
Well,

00:17:33.134 --> 00:17:35.336
I think we've got to look at what's come before as well.

00:17:35.376 --> 00:17:40.822
So it could be that there have been confrontations like this in the past where people have taken weapons with them and nobody's got hurt,

00:17:40.862 --> 00:17:41.623
no one's died.

00:17:41.702 --> 00:17:43.844
Somebody may have ended up with a minor injury,

00:17:44.204 --> 00:17:48.568
but actually it hasn't ended up being a big deal and I think often there's the expectation that,

00:17:48.588 --> 00:17:48.709
well,

00:17:48.769 --> 00:17:50.610
nothing serious is going to really happen.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:52.511
This is just a bit of a rumble.

00:17:52.751 --> 00:17:54.634
But then when you've got them in the crowd situation,

00:17:54.634 --> 00:17:57.395
you also have a thing called risk dispersion.

00:17:57.615 --> 00:18:00.317
And what happens is that the more people you have,

00:18:00.498 --> 00:18:02.079
the risk gets dispersed.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:04.101
So one person wouldn't hit them,

00:18:04.422 --> 00:18:08.444
half a dozen people hit because they're all showing less and less responsibility.

00:18:08.625 --> 00:18:12.067
I think when you've got this discussion going on and there are lots of people involved in it,

00:18:12.367 --> 00:18:15.990
even when you are saying quite strong things,

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.712
like let's tool up and whatever,

00:18:18.712 --> 00:18:21.756
sometimes there isn't the feeling that that's actually going to happen.

00:18:22.111 --> 00:18:23.211
Perhaps it's bravado,

00:18:23.432 --> 00:18:29.053
perhaps it's people just engaging in this kind of honour contest and status and saying,

00:18:29.134 --> 00:18:30.193
look how big I am,

00:18:30.894 --> 00:18:34.975
that there isn't the feeling that this is ever going to really be something.

00:18:35.195 --> 00:18:39.096
And I think you often find that when you've got interaction in these virtual spaces.

00:18:39.136 --> 00:18:40.616
It doesn't feel quite real.

00:18:40.636 --> 00:18:45.378
It doesn't feel like it's going to turn into embodied face-to-face violence.

00:18:45.379 --> 00:18:46.158
It's just talk.

00:18:46.759 --> 00:18:48.438
So why didn't anyone object?

00:18:48.638 --> 00:18:50.279
Why didn't anybody in that collective say...

00:18:50.847 --> 00:18:51.107
Guys,

00:18:51.148 --> 00:18:52.429
this is getting a bit out of hand.

00:18:52.609 --> 00:18:55.171
Because they didn't think it was getting out of hand.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:56.392
They're going there,

00:18:56.432 --> 00:18:57.393
they're going to have a rumble,

00:18:57.673 --> 00:19:00.153
they're going to show the other side who's boss and things like that.

00:19:00.414 --> 00:19:01.414
That's what it's all about.

00:19:01.475 --> 00:19:03.076
They just see a bit of a rumble,

00:19:03.477 --> 00:19:04.257
we're going to win,

00:19:04.336 --> 00:19:06.399
we'll put the other ones in their place and that's it.

00:19:10.741 --> 00:19:13.023
On a spring day in 2010,

00:19:13.824 --> 00:19:19.827
schoolboy Safian Belamouaden was brutally murdered in a fight between two rival gangs of teenagers.

00:19:20.268 --> 00:19:21.609
At Victoria Station.

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:22.410
When

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:27.033
15-year-old Sofian Belmawadin headed off for school on March 25th,

00:19:27.073 --> 00:19:28.094
2010,

00:19:28.394 --> 00:19:33.037
he had no idea that this would be the last time he would make that journey.

00:19:33.738 --> 00:19:35.439
It was just a normal day.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:35.879
He got up,

00:19:35.939 --> 00:19:40.022
got ready for school around 7 and left by 7.30.

00:19:42.124 --> 00:19:47.968
Tensions between two rival groups of teenagers from different schools had built to a fever pitch.

00:19:48.307 --> 00:19:51.151
and he would be the fatal casualty of a turf war.

00:19:51.932 --> 00:19:53.794
He wasn't the type to get involved in fights,

00:19:53.854 --> 00:19:56.856
but he was always with his friends,

00:19:56.957 --> 00:19:59.118
so if his friend had a fight,

00:19:59.799 --> 00:19:59.960
he'll...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.020
Obviously help his friend.

00:20:02.021 --> 00:20:06.402
Sofian had gone to the Henry Compton School for Boys in Film and the day before,

00:20:06.662 --> 00:20:10.803
one of his fellow classmates had punched a kid from St Charles'

00:20:10.923 --> 00:20:14.564
College and that had stirred up some more bad blood between them.

00:20:16.183 --> 00:20:16.944
The St Charles'

00:20:17.025 --> 00:20:19.825
students were now desperate for revenge.

00:20:23.165 --> 00:20:24.046
The previous night,

00:20:24.185 --> 00:20:25.307
as soon as they got home,

00:20:25.527 --> 00:20:26.426
the St Charles'

00:20:26.467 --> 00:20:29.567
pupils spread the news about the punch on social media.

00:20:30.579 --> 00:20:31.019
Two of them,

00:20:31.361 --> 00:20:33.922
Samson Odigbune and Victoria Osoteku,

00:20:34.222 --> 00:20:36.663
spent most of the evening stirring up trouble.

00:20:37.585 --> 00:20:38.585
And the following morning,

00:20:38.806 --> 00:20:40.967
more messages were exchanged at school.

00:20:41.406 --> 00:20:44.348
The pressure to exact retribution was increasing.

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:45.650
Intriguingly,

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:48.612
about four miles from the St Charles Sixth Form College,

00:20:48.932 --> 00:20:49.913
at Sothian School,

00:20:50.313 --> 00:20:56.898
Sothian took time out during his lunch hour to call his mother to complain about feeling unwell and asking to come home.

00:20:57.038 --> 00:20:58.719
I have a headache and my stomach hurts.

00:20:59.460 --> 00:20:59.960
Can I go home?

00:21:00.347 --> 00:21:00.728
His mother,

00:21:00.748 --> 00:21:01.068
however,

00:21:01.128 --> 00:21:04.290
persuaded him to stay at school until the end of the day.

00:21:04.632 --> 00:21:09.755
We'll never know if Safian realized that something was brewing and didn't want anything to do with it.

00:21:10.115 --> 00:21:10.797
What we do know,

00:21:10.856 --> 00:21:11.257
however,

00:21:11.496 --> 00:21:15.619
is that Victoria Osoteku knew and wanted a fight.

00:21:15.901 --> 00:21:16.740
She was up for it.

00:21:17.021 --> 00:21:19.884
And at the same time as Safian was calling his mother,

00:21:20.243 --> 00:21:23.586
she was at this Argos store buying a set of knives.

00:21:25.268 --> 00:21:27.690
Victoria Osoteku bought a set,

00:21:27.931 --> 00:21:29.471
a £3.99 set.

00:21:30.131 --> 00:21:39.815
...of kitchen knives with serrated edges from Argus in her lunch break that day as a result of the social media exchanges the night before.

00:21:40.174 --> 00:21:47.116
This was going to be her contribution to ensure that she was arming the side of the gang and to encourage others to join in.

00:21:47.456 --> 00:21:51.258
She wanted to play a part in ensuring that the gang were well armed,

00:21:51.717 --> 00:21:53.538
ready and able to commit the violence.

00:21:54.678 --> 00:21:56.879
She was the eldest of the group,

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.299
she was 18 years old.

00:21:59.087 --> 00:22:05.472
There's obviously become much tighter restrictions on teenagers buying knives because of the number of teenagers murdered,

00:22:06.553 --> 00:22:16.640
often after school with knives and they obviously felt that Victoria would be the person who would be able to get them unchallenged and then equip them for this battle.

00:22:31.563 --> 00:22:34.706
Victoria Oseteku reminds me of a modern-day

00:22:35.107 --> 00:22:36.249
Lady Macbeth,

00:22:36.648 --> 00:22:40.372
inciting violence and then providing the weapons to enact it.

00:22:41.033 --> 00:22:42.414
But like so many of her friends,

00:22:42.755 --> 00:22:44.917
she had no criminal record to speak of.

00:22:45.458 --> 00:22:47.179
So what made a young woman,

00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:49.041
with her whole life ahead of her,

00:22:49.322 --> 00:22:52.665
become actively involved in a murderous enterprise?

00:22:55.935 --> 00:23:03.461
Osuteko had had a difficult childhood and she'd been in care and clearly not the best start in life for a young woman.

00:23:04.363 --> 00:23:13.990
But Osuteko was somebody who had learned relatively early on the power of manipulation and the power of boasting and putting up a front,

00:23:14.270 --> 00:23:15.152
putting up an image.

00:23:16.192 --> 00:23:22.278
When she gets a role in school as this gangster girl,

00:23:22.678 --> 00:23:23.459
Missy Mafia,

00:23:24.319 --> 00:23:24.480
She

00:23:25.139 --> 00:23:26.923
Takes that and she runs with it.

00:23:27.443 --> 00:23:29.165
She wants to be accepted by the boys.

00:23:29.386 --> 00:23:34.875
She wants to be feared She likes fighting it gives her a sense of belonging

00:23:35.563 --> 00:23:37.464
We see that with people who join gangs.

00:23:37.844 --> 00:23:39.164
They call it street families.

00:23:39.764 --> 00:23:43.505
They seek something in their peers that they haven't got at home,

00:23:43.945 --> 00:23:46.466
and I think that explains her really well.

00:23:46.606 --> 00:23:48.547
She's seeking out something that she hasn't had.

00:23:50.167 --> 00:23:51.988
On the day of Sofian's murder,

00:23:52.588 --> 00:23:56.729
fevered messages continued to fly back and forth via BlackBerry Messenger.

00:23:57.569 --> 00:24:03.611
Events were beginning to spiral out of control and the inevitability of a serious conflict grew.

00:24:04.503 --> 00:24:05.263
During the day,

00:24:05.563 --> 00:24:10.925
the heat from the online chatter was adding to the already febrile atmosphere.

00:24:11.645 --> 00:24:13.006
The barrage of gossip,

00:24:13.126 --> 00:24:20.608
rumours and threats added to social media bravado built to a clamour for bloodletting and violence throughout the day.

00:24:21.369 --> 00:24:24.690
Messaging on social media kept on ramping it up.

00:24:26.610 --> 00:24:27.431
This is going to happen,

00:24:27.571 --> 00:24:28.271
this is going to happen.

00:24:29.091 --> 00:24:29.812
Bring weapons,

00:24:29.813 --> 00:24:30.292
bring knives,

00:24:30.452 --> 00:24:30.613
bring...

00:24:30.614 --> 00:24:30.812
Er...

00:24:31.574 --> 00:24:31.854
Thanks.

00:24:32.493 --> 00:24:33.234
This is going to happen.

00:24:35.076 --> 00:24:37.498
By the end of the school day at 3.15,

00:24:37.837 --> 00:24:40.899
there was an expectation of imminent violence.

00:24:41.220 --> 00:24:50.686
Osseteku and Odig Bone and some of the other students at St Charles College here believed that there was going to be a fight actually outside the school gates.

00:24:51.086 --> 00:24:51.366
However,

00:24:51.406 --> 00:24:52.407
when they came outside,

00:24:52.728 --> 00:24:53.828
there was no-one to be seen.

00:24:54.088 --> 00:24:57.872
They then get a call indicating that their Henry Compton school rivals...

00:24:58.255 --> 00:25:00.076
were headed towards Victoria.

00:25:00.376 --> 00:25:09.301
They seized the opportunity to take revenge for the previous day's loss of faith and headed en masse to Victoria for a bloody fight.

00:25:12.043 --> 00:25:12.624
Meanwhile,

00:25:12.923 --> 00:25:15.725
Sofian and his friends were hanging out after school.

00:25:16.306 --> 00:25:17.366
He was with a group of boys.

00:25:17.906 --> 00:25:18.887
He acted normal,

00:25:19.387 --> 00:25:19.747
nothing.

00:25:19.928 --> 00:25:20.628
When I saw him,

00:25:20.729 --> 00:25:22.029
there was nothing different about him.

00:25:23.410 --> 00:25:25.811
But Sofian was hiding something from his sister.

00:25:26.255 --> 00:25:26.855
In reality,

00:25:27.096 --> 00:25:33.117
he'd arranged to meet up with his school friends so they could go to Victoria and confront the St Charles gang.

00:25:33.457 --> 00:25:35.938
He put his arm around me and he said to them,

00:25:36.118 --> 00:25:37.118
this is my little sister,

00:25:37.838 --> 00:25:38.499
take care of her.

00:25:39.779 --> 00:25:41.099
And then I was like...

00:25:41.100 --> 00:25:42.139
I just felt normal,

00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:43.500
I didn't think of it as anything.

00:25:43.600 --> 00:25:43.880
And then

00:25:44.880 --> 00:25:49.162
I went upstairs and the 72 bus came.

00:25:49.163 --> 00:25:50.762
That's the bus we get on to go home.

00:25:51.883 --> 00:25:52.342
And then

00:25:53.383 --> 00:25:54.943
I looked down at him and I was like to him,

00:25:55.003 --> 00:25:55.503
what's he feeling like?

00:25:56.135 --> 00:25:56.496
Come on,

00:25:56.635 --> 00:25:57.296
the bus is here.

00:25:58.457 --> 00:25:59.017
And he's like,

00:25:59.018 --> 00:25:59.396
go home,

00:25:59.436 --> 00:26:00.198
I'll see you at home,

00:26:00.258 --> 00:26:01.657
and that was the last time I spoke to him.

00:26:04.859 --> 00:26:08.221
The St Charles gang travelled to Victoria on two buses.

00:26:09.040 --> 00:26:11.442
Some even flashed their weapons to one another on the bus,

00:26:11.922 --> 00:26:17.305
seemingly oblivious to the fact that CCTV cameras were recording their every move.

00:26:18.464 --> 00:26:19.526
There was so much

00:26:20.006 --> 00:26:23.426
CCTV available all the way along the line.

00:26:23.826 --> 00:26:24.386
From the moment

00:26:24.768 --> 00:26:25.248
St Charles...

00:26:25.883 --> 00:26:29.585
Gang was on the bus to arrive at Victoria Station.

00:26:29.985 --> 00:26:31.745
The whole stampede across

00:26:32.166 --> 00:26:33.886
Timeless Place outside Victoria Station,

00:26:34.246 --> 00:26:35.587
all covered by CCTV.

00:26:36.487 --> 00:26:39.289
You couldn't pick a worse place in Britain,

00:26:39.369 --> 00:26:40.389
perhaps the world,

00:26:40.769 --> 00:26:43.750
to try and commit an act of violence in public.

00:26:43.810 --> 00:26:49.353
There are more CCTV cameras at Victoria Railway Station than perhaps anywhere else on earth.

00:26:49.513 --> 00:26:51.273
It's up the road from Buckingham Palace,

00:26:51.454 --> 00:26:54.815
it's a main transit hub for the whole of south-west London.

00:26:55.115 --> 00:26:56.296
There's an underground station,

00:26:56.416 --> 00:26:57.657
Parliament's down the road.

00:26:57.997 --> 00:27:00.879
It is a security centre for the UK.

00:27:02.300 --> 00:27:09.725
This suggests partly that we are dealing with teenagers who are not sophisticated in their planning.

00:27:10.606 --> 00:27:12.367
The planning was intense,

00:27:12.787 --> 00:27:15.429
but it omits the major fact which older,

00:27:15.689 --> 00:27:18.031
more hardened criminals would have spotted straight away.

00:27:18.892 --> 00:27:22.654
The St Charles group arrived at Victoria Station just after

00:27:23.095 --> 00:27:23.455
5pm.

00:27:24.236 --> 00:27:26.057
Among them was Samson Odigbune.

00:27:27.037 --> 00:27:30.338
While large numbers of the group were carrying knives and screwdrivers,

00:27:30.858 --> 00:27:33.920
Odigbune was wielding a samurai sword.

00:27:34.500 --> 00:27:35.901
In a peer pressure environment,

00:27:36.221 --> 00:27:38.061
such as mobs or gangs,

00:27:38.742 --> 00:27:39.903
you've got one-upmanship.

00:27:40.403 --> 00:27:41.163
I'll bring a knife,

00:27:41.183 --> 00:27:41.804
well I'll bring...

00:27:42.497 --> 00:27:43.458
A samurai sword.

00:27:45.339 --> 00:27:45.459
So

00:27:45.879 --> 00:27:47.000
I've got a bigger knife than you.

00:27:47.941 --> 00:27:48.121
Now,

00:27:48.902 --> 00:27:54.005
the initial indication of using that weapon may be just to scare.

00:27:55.146 --> 00:27:56.647
But then if someone gets trapped,

00:27:57.008 --> 00:27:57.628
isolated,

00:27:57.748 --> 00:27:59.129
like predator and prey,

00:27:59.970 --> 00:28:01.331
all of a sudden the rage,

00:28:01.351 --> 00:28:02.231
the anger's there,

00:28:02.371 --> 00:28:04.073
the rational thinking has gone,

00:28:04.693 --> 00:28:05.754
and someone's trapped,

00:28:06.494 --> 00:28:09.757
and that's when we usually find severe violence and...

00:28:10.077 --> 00:28:11.178
even murder can occur.

00:28:14.841 --> 00:28:17.883
CCTV footage showed around 40 in the St.

00:28:17.923 --> 00:28:18.364
Charles'

00:28:18.464 --> 00:28:19.204
college group.

00:28:19.605 --> 00:28:21.306
The adrenaline must have been racing,

00:28:21.526 --> 00:28:24.889
and it was clear that a flashpoint was fast approaching.

00:28:25.289 --> 00:28:26.711
At around 20 past five,

00:28:27.131 --> 00:28:33.376
Sofian's Henry Compton group approached from the Apollo Theatre direction on the eastern side of the station,

00:28:33.776 --> 00:28:36.819
gesturing and shouting and clearly up for a fight.

00:28:37.019 --> 00:28:38.600
The only problem was the St.

00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:39.141
Charles'

00:28:39.241 --> 00:28:39.441
group...

00:28:39.725 --> 00:28:42.446
...had superior numbers and were better armed.

00:28:42.866 --> 00:28:45.407
Led by Oded Bunne and his samurai sword,

00:28:45.667 --> 00:28:47.508
the rest of his crew had knives,

00:28:47.728 --> 00:28:49.469
machetes and screwdrivers.

00:28:49.989 --> 00:28:51.730
Outnumbered and out-armed,

00:28:52.070 --> 00:28:54.071
Sophian schoolmates did a runner.

00:28:55.531 --> 00:29:00.914
CCTV images show the St Charles students charging at the Henry Compton pupils.

00:29:01.634 --> 00:29:04.535
The charge is led by Oded Bunne with a samurai sword,

00:29:04.575 --> 00:29:05.896
a most fearsome weapon,

00:29:06.356 --> 00:29:07.396
barging people out of the way,

00:29:07.636 --> 00:29:08.957
scattering them in their wake.

00:29:09.605 --> 00:29:10.466
Screaming and yelling.

00:29:11.406 --> 00:29:14.388
Just behind Odi Gbune was Victoria Osoteku,

00:29:14.949 --> 00:29:15.689
and following them,

00:29:16.010 --> 00:29:18.731
the rest of the armed St Charles gang.

00:29:21.633 --> 00:29:22.854
In the ensuing chaos,

00:29:23.135 --> 00:29:25.236
the Henry Compton students scattered.

00:29:26.357 --> 00:29:29.299
Most of the Henry Compton group made good their escape,

00:29:29.559 --> 00:29:36.224
but Sofian had split from his friends and found himself dangerously isolated at the top of the stairs.

00:29:36.904 --> 00:29:37.124
Scream

00:29:39.777 --> 00:29:40.117
The St.

00:29:40.157 --> 00:29:45.920
Charles group spotted him and suddenly made him the focus of their maelstrom of aggression and hate.

00:29:51.042 --> 00:29:54.463
He became interlocked with the attackers and tumbled down the stairs.

00:29:54.823 --> 00:29:56.124
At the very bottom of the stairs,

00:29:56.404 --> 00:29:58.845
the mob descended on the defenseless

00:29:59.205 --> 00:29:59.645
Sofian

00:29:59.985 --> 00:30:00.666
Belamouaden.

00:30:01.886 --> 00:30:02.947
He had no chance.

00:30:09.809 --> 00:30:14.555
Victoria Ostateko was watching this horrendous violence with glee.

00:30:16.277 --> 00:30:17.659
This is what she had wanted.

00:30:18.440 --> 00:30:20.242
As her friends fled,

00:30:21.223 --> 00:30:25.809
she sorted over to the body of Sofian and kicked him with her foot.

00:30:40.217 --> 00:30:42.378
The attack lasted just 12 seconds,

00:30:42.658 --> 00:30:46.179
but it was long enough for Sofyan to be stabbed nine times.

00:30:46.500 --> 00:30:50.761
One blow to his right shoulder was 12 centimeters deep and sliced through a lung.

00:30:51.061 --> 00:30:52.182
Two blows hit a leg.

00:30:52.442 --> 00:30:55.663
Another shattered his ribcage and wounded his heart.

00:30:56.023 --> 00:30:58.524
Other blows damaged major blood vessels.

00:31:02.485 --> 00:31:04.586
As Sofyan lay critically injured,

00:31:04.827 --> 00:31:05.547
a reverend,

00:31:05.867 --> 00:31:07.108
Canon Anthony Bowell,

00:31:07.368 --> 00:31:11.731
made his way through the crowds of horrified commuters to comfort him.

00:31:12.372 --> 00:31:17.235
I was just walking up the corridor and I saw a kid struggling.

00:31:17.315 --> 00:31:17.756
to get up,

00:31:17.916 --> 00:31:26.106
surrounded by three or four others who were kicking him and making a stabbing motion that

00:31:26.666 --> 00:31:29.189
I thought was just kind of someone hitting at the time.

00:31:29.790 --> 00:31:32.273
What happened as you approached Safi on the ground?

00:31:32.753 --> 00:31:37.817
He was trying to get up and he was being kicked and hit.

00:31:38.578 --> 00:31:42.501
What subsequently I discovered was being stabbed.

00:31:43.522 --> 00:31:45.684
And as I approached,

00:31:46.785 --> 00:31:54.251
the teenagers around him kind of turned around and fled up some stairs that were just behind where he was.

00:31:54.831 --> 00:31:56.813
And you were holding him as he was dying.

00:31:56.833 --> 00:31:57.914
Were you holding his hand?

00:31:58.534 --> 00:31:58.674
Yeah,

00:31:59.055 --> 00:32:01.296
I was holding his hand.

00:32:01.356 --> 00:32:02.097
sometimes

00:32:02.838 --> 00:32:03.618
his shoulder,

00:32:04.099 --> 00:32:06.761
but his eyes had grazed over.

00:32:06.781 --> 00:32:08.743
He wasn't really connected.

00:32:08.783 --> 00:32:12.488
That's what I was anxious to try and sort of get some connection,

00:32:12.627 --> 00:32:12.807
but

00:32:14.069 --> 00:32:16.371
I think he was unconscious by that point.

00:32:17.633 --> 00:32:19.815
The emergency services were called,

00:32:20.475 --> 00:32:21.576
but it was too late.

00:32:23.813 --> 00:32:26.617
The paramedics brought Sofyan to nearby St.

00:32:26.657 --> 00:32:27.097
Thomas'

00:32:27.157 --> 00:32:27.578
Hospital,

00:32:27.878 --> 00:32:30.201
where he was pronounced dead within the hour.

00:32:33.285 --> 00:32:34.166
After the attack,

00:32:34.407 --> 00:32:34.807
the St.

00:32:34.867 --> 00:32:36.890
Charles pupils fled the scene.

00:32:37.571 --> 00:32:40.995
A number of them headed straight for a bus to try and make their getaway.

00:32:43.578 --> 00:32:46.140
They then realized that many of them were still carrying their weapons.

00:32:46.680 --> 00:32:49.343
And when the police headed the bus off,

00:32:49.503 --> 00:32:50.143
stopped the bus,

00:32:50.684 --> 00:32:53.026
they had to dispose of the weapons pretty smartish.

00:32:53.486 --> 00:32:56.068
Some of them went out of the emergency back window.

00:32:56.388 --> 00:32:57.649
The police were able to hoover them up.

00:32:57.829 --> 00:33:02.814
Others kicked them and pushed them under seats on the upper deck or the lower deck.

00:33:03.354 --> 00:33:03.614
Again,

00:33:03.615 --> 00:33:06.336
the police were able to then recover this weaponry.

00:33:07.077 --> 00:33:09.818
They were arrested very swiftly afterwards by police,

00:33:10.138 --> 00:33:12.519
because Victoria has a lot of police around it,

00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:13.400
and again,

00:33:13.580 --> 00:33:15.561
everyone was arrested within a matter of minutes.

00:33:16.001 --> 00:33:16.201
Again,

00:33:16.221 --> 00:33:19.842
I think that shows the naivety of these children.

00:33:19.963 --> 00:33:22.123
They thought they would make their getaway on a bus.

00:33:23.204 --> 00:33:23.584
However,

00:33:23.664 --> 00:33:29.006
there was one key member of the group who did manage to escape the scene without being caught.

00:33:29.707 --> 00:33:34.449
Victoria Osoteku was one of the only ones who wasn't arrested at the scene of the crime.

00:33:35.049 --> 00:33:37.610
But instead of deciding to keep a low profile,

00:33:37.950 --> 00:33:43.612
she actually went to school the next day and began boasting about what she'd been involved in the day before.

00:33:43.972 --> 00:33:50.754
There was a school outing to the Victorian Albert Museum and she was so full of what had happened,

00:33:51.034 --> 00:33:52.474
so excited by what had happened,

00:33:52.734 --> 00:34:00.497
so gloating about her part in the murder that she couldn't stop bragging about it to her school friends.

00:34:01.437 --> 00:34:05.240
This schoolgirl's role in this violent murder is truly shocking.

00:34:06.041 --> 00:34:09.984
What do experts Mike Berry and Dr Liz Yardley make of Aseteku?

00:34:10.605 --> 00:34:13.667
One of the most extraordinary figures in this case is Victoria Aseteku,

00:34:14.048 --> 00:34:16.770
and she seemed to wind up a lot of the participants,

00:34:16.771 --> 00:34:17.791
and yet she was a woman,

00:34:18.091 --> 00:34:19.292
she was there at the scene.

00:34:19.512 --> 00:34:25.137
It's an unusual kind of ringmaster in this particular terribly violent crime.

00:34:25.797 --> 00:34:29.180
One interesting thing is we're finding more and more women being violent.

00:34:29.480 --> 00:34:30.301
They're violent...

00:34:30.461 --> 00:34:33.625
gangs of women in all the major cities in the UK now.

00:34:33.905 --> 00:34:41.032
She seems to have adopted the role of the leader and the one that's instigating it by using the social media,

00:34:41.072 --> 00:34:43.394
which she's done extremely well.

00:34:43.514 --> 00:34:48.038
She's really wound up these kids to get behind her,

00:34:48.597 --> 00:34:50.000
and she's done that very successfully.

00:34:50.420 --> 00:34:50.639
I mean,

00:34:50.900 --> 00:34:52.662
she knew exactly what buttons to push,

00:34:52.702 --> 00:34:53.123
didn't she?

00:34:53.663 --> 00:34:56.826
She knew exactly what things to say that would get people riled up.

00:34:57.133 --> 00:35:00.456
And I think when you have an environment like the online environment,

00:35:00.776 --> 00:35:03.979
when you're in a virtual type of communication,

00:35:04.920 --> 00:35:14.848
you are likely to be more extreme and more violent and more graphic than you would be if you were in the lunch hall at college saying,

00:35:14.868 --> 00:35:15.008
well,

00:35:15.229 --> 00:35:16.810
how are we going to have this fight?

00:35:16.870 --> 00:35:17.831
How is it going to happen?

00:35:18.111 --> 00:35:20.233
I think when you're not face-to-face,

00:35:20.253 --> 00:35:23.516
you're going to be encouraging behaviour that is much more extreme.

00:35:28.005 --> 00:35:28.565
The death of

00:35:28.987 --> 00:35:42.795
15-year-old Sofiane Bellamawaden in 2010 here at Victoria train station after an assault by 20 youths truly shocked the commuters who witnessed it and the wider British public who saw it reported on the news.

00:35:44.277 --> 00:35:45.737
Sofiane was chased,

00:35:45.857 --> 00:35:49.819
beaten and stabbed in front of hundreds of horrified commuters.

00:35:50.440 --> 00:35:52.521
It all happened within a matter of seconds.

00:35:59.033 --> 00:36:02.474
The build-up to Safian's killing was captured on CCTV.

00:36:03.114 --> 00:36:03.794
That evidence,

00:36:04.055 --> 00:36:07.376
along with footage of a fight between the two groups the day before,

00:36:07.676 --> 00:36:11.557
meant it didn't take long for the police to track down the suspects.

00:36:12.097 --> 00:36:18.439
The police realised very quickly that because there was so much evidence that all the children had travelled together,

00:36:18.979 --> 00:36:24.621
they'd all been involved in social media messaging or buying knives or distributing the knives.

00:36:25.017 --> 00:36:31.020
That they all must have had a very good idea that there was going to be a very violent confrontation that day at Victoria.

00:36:31.521 --> 00:36:38.364
20 St Charles College students were charged with murder under a legal principle called joint enterprise.

00:36:38.985 --> 00:36:47.209
This law allows defendants to be charged with offences they didn't personally commit if they can be shown to have taken an active and willing part.

00:36:48.049 --> 00:36:48.990
And under those laws,

00:36:49.050 --> 00:36:51.611
that means that everybody can be charged with the murder,

00:36:52.112 --> 00:36:54.313
even if they didn't actually deliver.

00:36:54.577 --> 00:36:55.938
A fatal blow themselves.

00:36:57.681 --> 00:36:59.661
This is a very controversial arm of the law,

00:37:00.302 --> 00:37:12.492
which basically allows the jury to consider whether a gang could all be charged with the most serious crime on the basis that they knew something was going to happen.

00:37:15.215 --> 00:37:20.518
It was the biggest joint enterprise prosecution ever in the courts in England and Wales.

00:37:20.619 --> 00:37:23.581
Four trials lasting over 21 months here.

00:37:23.905 --> 00:37:25.026
At the Old Bailey.

00:37:25.546 --> 00:37:25.966
In the end,

00:37:25.967 --> 00:37:29.949
the judge handed down three murder convictions and five for manslaughter.

00:37:30.289 --> 00:37:32.491
Others were convicted of lesser charges.

00:37:32.811 --> 00:37:33.351
In total,

00:37:33.611 --> 00:37:36.893
the defendants received 135 years in jail.

00:37:41.456 --> 00:37:42.497
By the time the case...

00:37:43.097 --> 00:37:45.778
17 teenagers had been sentenced to prison,

00:37:47.059 --> 00:37:47.519
among them

00:37:47.919 --> 00:37:48.640
Obi Nwake.

00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:50.040
Before his arrest,

00:37:50.060 --> 00:37:52.481
he did charity work alongside his studies.

00:37:53.141 --> 00:38:00.725
Nwake was sentenced to life with a minimum of 18 years for murder and conspiracy to commit grievous bodily harm.

00:38:01.865 --> 00:38:08.608
Also sentenced to 18 years for murder and conspiracy to commit grievous bodily harm was Christopher Omorigi,

00:38:09.188 --> 00:38:09.668
one of St.

00:38:09.728 --> 00:38:10.249
Charles'

00:38:10.269 --> 00:38:11.169
star pupils.

00:38:11.821 --> 00:38:16.222
The prosecution said Omorigi stabbed Safian as he lay on the floor.

00:38:17.543 --> 00:38:24.165
But the third and final murder conviction was handed down to a pupil who didn't even land a single blow.

00:38:25.445 --> 00:38:35.408
One of the most surprising aspects of the prosecution is that Samson Odigbune was convicted of murder despite never entering Victoria Station on the day of the murder and being nowhere near

00:38:35.748 --> 00:38:37.468
Safian when he was stabbed to death.

00:38:37.869 --> 00:38:39.249
Now the jury did convict him.

00:38:39.489 --> 00:38:45.091
because he was seen brandishing a samurai sword earlier that day and was seen to be inciting violence.

00:38:48.832 --> 00:38:54.954
Another of the St Charles gang seen to be inciting violence was Victoria Oseteku.

00:38:57.275 --> 00:39:05.037
She came before the court to try and create an impression that she was a poor girl who'd found herself just...

00:39:06.541 --> 00:39:17.750
Wrapped up in something that she had no idea was ever going to take place and then suddenly her friends did something which she never expected and she was frozen in the shock of the moment.

00:39:19.292 --> 00:39:20.753
When I saw her at the court hearing,

00:39:21.113 --> 00:39:23.755
she looked at her family and said,

00:39:23.936 --> 00:39:24.496
she mimed,

00:39:24.536 --> 00:39:25.036
I love you,

00:39:26.237 --> 00:39:26.398
and

00:39:27.138 --> 00:39:31.101
I got really angry because you get still to say that,

00:39:31.302 --> 00:39:31.482
but

00:39:32.102 --> 00:39:35.065
I can't hear that word again and I can't say it to my brother.

00:39:38.893 --> 00:39:40.494
In February 2012,

00:39:40.495 --> 00:39:45.017
Victoria Osoteku was convicted of manslaughter after a five-month trial.

00:39:45.417 --> 00:39:51.361
She was found to have orchestrated the fight on social media and to have bought the knives used in the attack.

00:39:51.682 --> 00:39:57.305
She was at the epicentre of the violence and even kicked Sofie in the head while he lay on the ground.

00:39:57.726 --> 00:40:02.069
She told the jury she only nudged his head with her foot to see if he was alright.

00:40:02.529 --> 00:40:04.270
The jury didn't believe her.

00:40:05.091 --> 00:40:08.393
So what do experts Dr Liz Yardley and Mike Berry

00:40:08.753 --> 00:40:10.535
make of this intriguing case?

00:40:11.796 --> 00:40:12.517
As criminologists,

00:40:12.518 --> 00:40:16.901
we try to categorise murderers in order to prevent future offences.

00:40:17.521 --> 00:40:21.265
What kind of social media murderers were these schoolchildren?

00:40:21.345 --> 00:40:24.288
I'd say that this fits the antagonistic category.

00:40:24.388 --> 00:40:31.554
So you've got the escalation of threats and of these kind of honour contests online.

00:40:31.555 --> 00:40:34.097
This is constant baiting of one another back and forth.

00:40:34.477 --> 00:40:37.699
And it escalates into face-to-face embodied violence.

00:40:37.779 --> 00:40:39.700
That's one thing about social media,

00:40:39.821 --> 00:40:41.422
is you send a message,

00:40:41.902 --> 00:40:43.403
if I'm awake and respond,

00:40:43.943 --> 00:40:45.264
you can get it back within seconds.

00:40:45.284 --> 00:40:46.085
And the other thing is,

00:40:46.225 --> 00:40:47.245
when they're giving messages,

00:40:47.386 --> 00:40:48.987
they're writing very short words,

00:40:49.347 --> 00:40:50.107
slang words,

00:40:50.367 --> 00:40:52.509
which gives you instant information,

00:40:52.929 --> 00:40:54.590
but doesn't give you a lot of discussion.

00:40:55.091 --> 00:40:56.892
And there's not a lot of thought going into it,

00:40:56.932 --> 00:40:57.292
other than,

00:40:57.652 --> 00:40:58.653
here is my message.

00:40:59.341 --> 00:41:09.985
It seemed to me that the social media accelerated things so quickly and that it weaponized the event that there was no time or room for anybody to intervene or put the brakes upon it.

00:41:10.266 --> 00:41:10.446
Well,

00:41:10.447 --> 00:41:19.449
I think what social media did in this example is to set the expectation to say this is going to happen and by having that out there,

00:41:19.450 --> 00:41:21.870
there's this idea of data permanence.

00:41:22.010 --> 00:41:23.931
So everybody's looking at their messenger going,

00:41:23.991 --> 00:41:24.111
oh,

00:41:24.251 --> 00:41:25.852
so apparently this thing's going to happen.

00:41:26.352 --> 00:41:28.293
And whereas when things are said...

00:41:28.573 --> 00:41:28.713
Yeah,

00:41:28.714 --> 00:41:29.313
it might happen,

00:41:29.333 --> 00:41:29.873
it might not.

00:41:30.234 --> 00:41:33.074
But I think it creates that expectation that this is going to come off.

00:41:33.134 --> 00:41:34.255
We are all going to be there,

00:41:34.375 --> 00:41:34.735
aren't we?

00:41:35.415 --> 00:41:39.336
And I think that did kind of secure the fact that this was going to come about.

00:41:39.916 --> 00:41:46.038
What safety net can anybody imagine or can you think of that would prevent a murder like this happening again?

00:41:46.798 --> 00:41:46.938
Well,

00:41:46.939 --> 00:41:48.559
I think we just need to take a very long,

00:41:48.639 --> 00:41:51.700
hard look at how young people are using social media,

00:41:51.920 --> 00:41:54.421
why are they using it and the ways that they're using it.

00:41:54.941 --> 00:41:55.421
And actually...

00:41:55.721 --> 00:41:58.703
Do we need to step back and ask any broader questions?

00:41:58.903 --> 00:42:07.509
So why are young men so prone to use violence to display their masculinity and a sense of status and a sense of honour?

00:42:07.689 --> 00:42:12.113
What is actually wrong with our society that means that this is something that's OK?

00:42:17.837 --> 00:42:20.839
I think what parents can do,

00:42:21.419 --> 00:42:23.521
and I know a lot of people are not going to like the sound of this.

00:42:24.333 --> 00:42:27.257
We have to be involved more with what our kids get up to.

00:42:27.898 --> 00:42:30.181
Because if we don't raise our kids,

00:42:30.762 --> 00:42:31.563
the gangs,

00:42:32.103 --> 00:42:32.864
peer pressure,

00:42:33.265 --> 00:42:35.648
social media would raise your kids for you.

00:42:36.169 --> 00:42:36.729
It means,

00:42:37.190 --> 00:42:37.931
as a society,

00:42:38.271 --> 00:42:41.976
we have to reflect back on ourselves and ask ourselves as parents,

00:42:42.517 --> 00:42:48.339
How can we be more of an influence on our kids than the social media,

00:42:48.639 --> 00:42:50.159
than peer pressure and gangs?

00:42:50.419 --> 00:42:52.460
How can we influence them more?

00:42:52.640 --> 00:43:09.145
And that is a very difficult process because it's already entrenched in this generation that social media and peer pressure and gangs are more inferential amongst certain groups of young people than parents are.

00:43:10.253 --> 00:43:10.693
Sadly,

00:43:10.813 --> 00:43:12.854
in the case of Safian Belomawaden,

00:43:13.134 --> 00:43:20.538
the world of social media created a situation that led to his death and to 17 teenagers being sent to prison.

00:43:21.638 --> 00:43:21.758
So,

00:43:21.818 --> 00:43:22.298
to this day,

00:43:22.338 --> 00:43:24.399
it hasn't hit me that he's gone.

00:43:24.419 --> 00:43:27.381
I know I can feel the pain and I feel that he's gone,

00:43:27.501 --> 00:43:27.681
but

00:43:28.541 --> 00:43:34.704
I always think that he just jumped on a train and he's on his way to this train that's never ending.

00:43:35.484 --> 00:43:36.985
One day it's going to end and he's going to come back.

00:43:38.877 --> 00:43:40.799
There's always going to be that pain in my heart,

00:43:40.879 --> 00:43:40.999
so...

00:43:43.801 --> 00:43:45.122
..that will never be taken away,

00:43:45.202 --> 00:43:45.322
so...

00:43:45.362 --> 00:43:47.083
It's always going to be there,

00:43:47.084 --> 00:43:48.264
no matter how old I get,

00:43:49.025 --> 00:43:49.905
how long it's been,

00:43:49.906 --> 00:43:51.406
it's always there.

00:43:51.407 --> 00:43:51.526
Sorry.

